---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/notes';

// Edit this list whenever the focus shifts, and bump the date.
// Each item: text before the link, the linked note's id and title, text after.
const currentlyUpdated = '2026-11-09';
const currently = [
  {
    before: 'Working through the open questions at the end of ',
    note: 'what-is-model-distillation',
    title: 'What is model distillation?',
    after: ', starting with forward vs. reverse KL vs. on-policy distillation for long-form generation.',
  },
  {
    before: 'Just wrote up ',
    note: 'reading-a-mccabe-thiele-diagram',
    title: 'McCabe–Thiele',
    after: ' end to end on a 50/50 feed, checked against Fenske and Gilliland.',
  },
  {
    before: 'Just worked through ',
    note: 'how-spirits-distillation-works',
    title: 'a stripping run and a spirit run',
    after: ' with real ethanol–water equilibrium data.',
  },
];
---

<Base title="About" description="Whose notebook this is, and why it’s called the 3-way distiller." current="about">
  <article class="entry">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I’m Sungmin. This is my notebook, kept in public mostly so that I
        write things down properly.
      </p>
      <p>
        The name comes from three kinds of distillation that have followed me around: training small
        language models to imitate large ones; separating mixtures in columns; and
        making spirits at home. All three are the same move. Take something complex and keep only what
        matters. That is also what I try to do in each entry here.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="about-block">
      <h2 class="label">Currently · updated <time datetime={currentlyUpdated}>{currentlyUpdated}</time></h2>
      <ul>
        {currently.map((c) => (
          <li>{c.before}<a href={href(`notes/${c.note}/`)}>{c.title}</a>{c.after}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="about-block about-block-quiet">
      <h2 class="label">How to read this</h2>
      <p>
        Entries marked <span class="rough">rough</span> are unfinished thinking and
        may be wrong. Longer entries open with a short distillate, so you can stop there.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="back"><a href={href()}>← index</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
